# This site publishes from the repository root. Adding functions added a
# dependency tree, and npm install puts it in that same root at build time, so
# it would otherwise be served. Nothing under here is ever a page.
# Verify on a deploy preview that /node_modules/ returns 404 before merging.
# The ! forces the rule. Without it Netlify serves an existing file in
# preference to a redirect, so package.json was returning 200 on the preview
# while node_modules 404'd on its own (it is never published).
/node_modules/*     /   404!
/package.json       /   404!
/package-lock.json  /   404!
/netlify.toml       /   404!

